# The herds pack (packs/herds): groups. Each herd starts with 20 animals;
# well fed, they calve, split when big and join when small; wolves take
# two at a bite. The grass sets how many there can be: about 50 000
# animals by the third day, then level, in a few hundred rows.
#
#   make run ARGS="scenario scenarios/tests/herds.scenario"
rules ../../packs/herds
seed 8
size 192 128
terrain water_level 0 rock_on_soil 0 rock_on_water 0
start herd 1 / 2000
start wolf 1 / 4000
start herd at (5, 5) with (heads = 150)
run 4d
expect eventually rows herd >= 30 to 1d        # big herds split
expect never rows herd > 1500                  # few rows for many heads: seen 1187 for 50 000
expect mean count herd >= 40000 from 3d        # the land's fill
expect never count herd > 60000                # and no more
expect eaten herd by wolf > 300                # two a bite
expect born herd > 30000                       # calves
expect traps herd == 0
expect traps wolf == 0
